## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | docs/agents/generated/pr_story_test_automation_review.md | ⚠️ important the sibling jira autostartrework chains stay unbounded — and the regenerated docs now claim the new knob covers them the pr caps the loop for the pr review leg postprreviewcomments js but at least three sibling jira actions trigger configured rework through the same autostartrework autostartreworkconfigfile knobs with their own trigger paths — none of which consult maxautoreworkrounds rework round n or needs human js poststorytestautomationreview js 86 101 — triggerrework postjsaction of pr story test automation review json and pr bug test automation review json fired unconditionally on a request changes verdict from triggeroutcomefollowup line 223 js poststorytestautomationshared js 177 182 — triggerautostartreworkworkflow pr test automation rework shared by the test review post actions js retrymergepr js 98 107 — triggerautostartrework the live pathology this pr fixes 22 alternating review rework legs on one ticket can recur unchanged through any of those legs this line makes it worse than a silent gap the regenerated doc lists maxautoreworkrounds used by js action for pr story test automation review and pr bug test automation review also docs agents generated pr bug test automation review md 110 the generator attributes it via the transitive require postprreviewcomments js in poststorytestautomationreview js 22 — but that action only borrows resolveapprovedthreads filterinlinecommentsbydiff from the module its rework path never reads the param a deployer configuring maxautoreworkrounds on this agent from the doc gets an uncapped loop — exactly the docs list knobs the job never reads failure mode gh 1346 fixed for plumbing modules suggested direction extract claimreworkround reworkroundof the needs human skip into a shared js common helper and route all four trigger paths through it or minimally drop the param rows from the two sibling docs and note the gap |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/postPRReviewComments.js | 💡 suggestion the round is stamped before the trigger outcome is known claimreworkround adds rework round n this line and only then does startconfiguredrework call triggerconfiguredrework autostart triggerconfiguredworkflowforticket has several guarded return false paths that are realistic in production js common autostart js 330 375 global workflow cap reached an active run already exists for the ticket ai target unresolvable on any of those the budget is consumed without a configured rework leg having started n consecutive trigger failures label the ticket needs human with zero successful auto reworks the sm fallback still fires so the ticket keeps moving — but the configured workflow the project opted into never ran stamping after a truthy trigger return makes rounds mean actual auto rework legs the counter argument for stamp first is crash safety a crash between dispatch and stamp would grant a free round still bounded per crash not unbounded either is defensible — please confirm the intended semantics or capture the choice in the claimreworkround comment so the next reader doesn t have to re derive it |
| F3 | open | SUGGESTION | js/postPRReviewComments.js | 💡 suggestion third copy of the rework round counting logic reworkroundof re implements countreworkrounds in js machinesmagent js 140 149 verbatim same rework round d regex same math max fold — that copy s own comment says it mirrors ai teammate yml max auto rework rounds bookkeeping the factory review verdict script carries a shell side variant too three implementations of one protocol means a label format change e g scoping rounds per pr must be synchronized in three places since both js copies live in this repo consider hoisting the helper into js common e g next to the ticket label helpers and requiring it from both actions with the github side default machinesmagent s maxreworkrounds currently 2 and this jira side default 3 passed by the callers so the shared function stays policy free |
| F4 | open | SUGGESTION | js/postPRReviewComments.js | 💡 suggestion maxautoreworkrounds 0 silently means 3 n 0 n default max auto rework rounds maps 0 — a value a deployer could reasonably use to mean never auto chain rework — to the 3 round default the documented disable knob is autostartrework false so the config still works but 0 inverting the obvious intent without a warning is a trap for exactly the deployers this doc row targets a one line console warn on a non positive value mirroring the legacyknobaudit style already in this file a doc clause in docs agents pr review md 21 or both would close it also untested neither the new tests nor characterization covers 0 non numeric values falling back to the default |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

